WEBVTT

NOTE Approximate script-based captions; no speech transcription or forced alignment.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.112
WorldForge brings warehouse design, route
planning and mobile robot simulation into

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:06.506
one web workspace.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.669
Start by describing the environment you want
to build.

00:00:09.669 --> 00:00:13.536
For example, a twenty by thirty metre
warehouse with storage racks

00:00:13.536 --> 00:00:14.239
and obstacles.

00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:19.406
Connect your own OpenAI API key for AI-
assisted building and editing.

00:00:19.406 --> 00:00:24.102
For this walkthrough, we'll open an existing
Astra-authored sample warehouse.

00:00:24.102 --> 00:00:29.539
Explore the layout, then choose the robot you
want to test.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.103
The clearance overlay shows the space it needs
around obstacles.

00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:36.408
Set a start and destination directly in the
scene, and plan

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:41.102
a route through the warehouse.

00:00:41.102 --> 00:00:44.721
Adjust a rack's dimensions, apply the edit,
and plan again to

00:00:44.721 --> 00:00:49.103
see how the layout changes the route.

00:00:49.103 --> 00:00:55.103
Now run the mission using planar MuJoCo
physics.

00:00:55.103 --> 00:01:01.262
Follow the robot through the warehouse, then
inspect the outcome.

00:01:01.262 --> 00:01:05.837
Review time, distance, contacts and clearance,
and replay the journey from

00:01:05.837 --> 00:01:08.102
different angles.

00:01:08.102 --> 00:01:12.322
WorldForge helps you explore warehouse layouts
and test robot missions before

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.240
moving to a physical setup.
